proof.text:
*Step 2: composing the operators and positive-exponent induction.* Write $\varphi^{[j]}:P_jK\to K$ for [def-trf-iterated-weil-map]. Naturality in [lem-trf-fixed-point-stalk-transport-cocycle], applied to $u=\varphi^{[b]}:P_bK\to K$, gives
$$(P_a\varphi^{[b]})_{\bar x}\circ t_{a,P_bK}=t_{a,K}\circ\varphi^{[b]}_{\bar x}.$$
For $a,b>0$ divisible by $d$, use [lem-trf-iterated-weil-cocycle] and Step 1 in the defining formula of [def-trf-frobenius-operators]:
$$\begin{aligned}
F_{z_{a+b},a+b}
&=\varphi^{[a]}_{\bar x}\circ(P_a\varphi^{[b]})_{\bar x}\circ t_{a,P_bK}\circ t_{b,K}\\
&=\varphi^{[a]}_{\bar x}\circ t_{a,K}\circ\varphi^{[b]}_{\bar x}\circ t_{b,K}
=F_{z_a,a}\circ F_{z_b,b}.
\end{aligned}$$
Induct on $r\geq1$ to prove $F_{z_{rd},rd}=F_x^r$. At $r=1$, $z_d=x_m$ and the equality is the definition of $F_x$. For $r>1$, apply the displayed composition law with $a=d$ and $b=(r-1)d>0$; the inductive hypothesis gives $F_{z_{rd},rd}=F_x\circ F_x^{r-1}=F_x^r$. No zero-level operator or zero-exponent Weil cocycle is invoked.
